nosco is an independent pure-Rust scholarly document extraction engine
compatible with GROBID 0.9.1 CRF models and lexicons. It is not officially
affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by the GROBID project.

========================================================================
Upstream Design & Compatibility Attributions
========================================================================

- GROBID (https://github.com/grobidOrg/grobid)
  Copyright Patrice Lopez and contributors.
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  nosco ports GROBID's CRF feature extractors, document segmentation
  cascade, and TEI P5 output conventions to pure Rust, and reads
  pre-trained models and lexicons from an upstream grobid-home directory.

- Wapiti (https://github.com/Jekub/Wapiti)
  Copyright Thomas Lavergne.
  Licensed under the BSD 2-Clause License.
  nosco-crf implements a pure-Rust linear-chain CRF decoder compatible
  with Wapiti's model format and Viterbi/forward-backward math.

